cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Russell 3000 Statistical Arbitrage — Pairs Trading Research System"
abstract: >-
  A cointegration pairs-trading research system over the Russell 3000: formation-period
  pair selection with point-in-time screens, a two-state Kalman hedge ratio, next-day
  fills with a per-stock cost model, a continuous walk-forward simulation, statistical
  significance testing (Probabilistic and Deflated Sharpe, Newey-West, block bootstrap,
  probability of backtest overfitting) and Gatev-distance / random-pair baselines run on
  the same footing. Version 32 rebuilt the engine after a full audit and is validated on
  synthetic markets with known answers. Its 2026-10-18 study run finds no edge:
  negative and not significant in sample and out of sample, no different from the
  baselines, and a learned ranker with no out-of-sample skill.
